PATCH 637: retain saved DOS handles across config reads and overlay size queries (board:0014).

Actual fefb is module0f69:086b, not a main-module CS inferred from its name.
Original ff0d saves open AX; ff1c restores it, ff21 moves it to BX for AH3e.
ff20 PUSHF /ff27 POPF retain read flags even after successful close. Preserve
that CF result in the existing interrupt return slot; full port flags/GP,
ES/caller state, stack, IRQ and instruction/device time remain open.
Original150d0 saves open AX and150dc restores BX after seek-to-end, then
150dd..150e4 preserve returned DX:AX around close. Use the saved handle,
not unrelated fefb param9 or50c8 param7. No guessed handle5 or high-word mask.

Fresh source reproduction: python3 -B tools/oracle/capture_file_close.py
--output /tmp/wasm-fist-file-close-source. The compact file_close_case.json
binds actual code, complete fetches, original sizes and unchanged39 frames/
27518 mixed samples/end600. The real DOS/file-owner regression reaches16
parent failures across Native/WASM: leaked handles, an unrelated peer closed,
wrong AX and lost read CF. Tests include independent handles, missing files,
short/full/empty reads and both seek size words. File lifetime/carry only;
no full original frames/PCM/CPU/time or settings op44 return acceptance.
